    "text": "Token Bucket: > Token bucket algorithm allows idle hosts to accumulate credit for the future in the form of tokens. > For each tick of the clock, the system sends(n Jokens to the bucket. > The system removes one token for every cell (or byte) of data sent. L lof / bli Example: if nis 100 and the host ts idle for 100 ticks, the bucket collects 10,000 tokens. > Now the host can consume all these tokens in one tick with 10,000 cells, or the host takes 1000 ticks with 10 cells per tick. The host can send bursty data as long as the bucket is not empty > Token bucket can be implemented with a counter. Token ts initialized to zero. > Each time a token 1s added, the counter ts incremented by 1. > Each time a unit of data 1s sent, the counter 1s decremented by 1. > When the counter is zero, the host cannot send data. > The token bucket allows bursty traffic at a regulated maximum rate.",
